<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Generalization gap results across model sizes and question set sizes. Values show gap percentages with 95% confidence intervals below. Negative gaps indicate smaller train–test gap (better generalization). Bold values indicate intervals that exclude zero at the 95% level, per the criterion in Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Experimental details ‣ 4 Results ‣ Optimizing for Persuasion Improves LLM Generalization: Evidence from Quality-Diversity Evolution of Debate Strategies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</figcaption>
